# `lti::StateSpace::inputs`

[Back to `lti::StateSpace`](../StateSpace.md)

The number of inputs, `m`.

## Signature

```cpp
std::int64_t lti::StateSpace::inputs() const;
```

## What It Does

Returns `m`, the number of inputs, read from the last dimension of `B`. It is the quickest way to size a vector or loop that accompanies the system without taking a matrix apart. The value is an integer count and does not depend on any batch axes.

## Returns

`m` as a non-negative integer.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

The oscillator has a single force input.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace lti = pluss::subsp::eng::lti;
using namespace pluss::tils;

static pluss::Series mat(std::vector<double> v, std::int64_t r, std::int64_t c) { return pluss::make_series(std::move(v), {r, c}); }
// A damped oscillator x'' + 0.4 x' + 4 x = u with the position as output.
static lti::StateSpace oscillator(double sample_time = 0.0) {
  return lti::state(mat({0.0, 1.0, -4.0, -0.4}, 2, 2), mat({0.0, 1.0}, 2, 1), mat({1.0, 0.0}, 1, 2), mat({0.0}, 1, 1), sample_time);
}

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  out.writeln("inputs =", oscillator().inputs());
}
```

### Example 2

Two input columns in `B` give two inputs.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace lti = pluss::subsp::eng::lti;
using namespace pluss::tils;

static pluss::Series mat(std::vector<double> v, std::int64_t r, std::int64_t c) { return pluss::make_series(std::move(v), {r, c}); }
// A damped oscillator x'' + 0.4 x' + 4 x = u with the position as output.
static lti::StateSpace oscillator(double sample_time = 0.0) {
  return lti::state(mat({0.0, 1.0, -4.0, -0.4}, 2, 2), mat({0.0, 1.0}, 2, 1), mat({1.0, 0.0}, 1, 2), mat({0.0}, 1, 1), sample_time);
}

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const lti::StateSpace s = lti::state(mat({0.0, 1.0, -4.0, -0.4}, 2, 2), mat({0.0, 0.0, 1.0, 1.0}, 2, 2), mat({1.0, 0.0}, 1, 2), mat({0.0, 0.0}, 1, 2));
  out.writeln("inputs =", s.inputs());
}
```

### Example 3

The input count is independent of the number of states.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace lti = pluss::subsp::eng::lti;
using namespace pluss::tils;

static pluss::Series mat(std::vector<double> v, std::int64_t r, std::int64_t c) { return pluss::make_series(std::move(v), {r, c}); }
// A damped oscillator x'' + 0.4 x' + 4 x = u with the position as output.
static lti::StateSpace oscillator(double sample_time = 0.0) {
  return lti::state(mat({0.0, 1.0, -4.0, -0.4}, 2, 2), mat({0.0, 1.0}, 2, 1), mat({1.0, 0.0}, 1, 2), mat({0.0}, 1, 1), sample_time);
}

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const lti::StateSpace s = oscillator();
  out.writeln("states =", s.states(), ", inputs =", s.inputs());
}
```

